WEBVTT

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:04.030
It's been a while since
we came to this island, but

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.900
there's no sign of a rescue team.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:09.220
It seems we're in this for the long haul,
so I was thinking of exploring the island.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.900
<b>Exploring the Island</b>

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:09.980
When?

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:11.150
Immediately.

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:12.320
Huh?

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.750
Fishing grounds, water sources, plants...

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:18.070
I'd like to see if things like a better camp
site than this and better driftwood exist.

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.680
And I'd like to prepare for
fall and winter, just in case.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.000
Y-You want to get ready
for that now? It's still far off...

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.130
Now, considering the risks,
I'd like someone to come with me.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.210
In that case, I'll go!

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:32.920
I'd like to go, too!

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:34.810
No, I only need one person.

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:37.720
We can't leave just one person
here at camp either.

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:39.350
Then, Homare...

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.260
Me or Mutsu? Who can you rely on?

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:43.310
Really?

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:44.930
It's me, right?

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:44.930
<i>Of course.</i>

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:46.100
No, no. It's me, isn't it?

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:47.570
<i>You can't depend on a useless partner, right?</i>

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.570
Oh, come on, Mutsu.

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:49.360
Now, now, Asuka-san...

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:49.730
<i>Of course you'd take someone
dependable with you.</i>

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:50.380
I'm th—

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:51.840
I suppose there's no helping it.

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:54.780
I wouldn't mind accompanying you.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:55.500
Huh?

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.390
Where does that confidence come from?

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.600
Now! Homare-san!

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:01.410
Who will you choose?

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:02.690
Uh...

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:12.670
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:15.470
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:06.180
<b>Water</b>

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:06.310
<b>Rope</b>

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:06.180
<b>Knife</b>

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:05.680
<b>Dried Rock Shell {TLC?}</b>

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:10.100
We're counting on you to look after the camp.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.250
We're off.

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:14.050
Bye, I guess.

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:15.660
Be careful.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:17.820
Wow, they seem unenthusiastic...

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:26.640
It's much easier walking over sand barefoot.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:30.180
It's hot, so it's best to walk
near the water where it's wet.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:30.790
Oh.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:33.210
It's beach silvertop.

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:35.230
You can eat it raw.

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:40.730
Since it's summer, it's tough.
The fibers stay in your mouth.

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:43.160
But it's crisp and delicious.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:45.010
Is it a Japanese plant?

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:48.600
This grows all over the world...

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:51.490
It wouldn't give you any clues
as to where you are.

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:52.650
I see...

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:58.740
I've been thinking that this island
is somewhere near Japan, but...

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:02.900
Some of the things that drift ashore
have labels in English or Chinese...

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:04.830
but Japanese is the most common, so...

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:08.490
If Japan is close, we can swim back.

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:12.000
<i>I wonder if she's joking...</i>

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:15.380
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:14.410
Really?

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.830
Careful not to slip.

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:21.590
Okay.

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:29.490
H-Homare-san!

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:32.170
Isn't that a dock for boats?

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:37.600
M-Maybe there are people around...

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:41.220
No. It looks like it's been
neglected for a long time.

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.210
There might be some kind of living space, too.

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:44.570
I'd like to find it.

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:47.280
And there might be someone there!

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:49.200
That's true.

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:51.870
But we shouldn't push ourselves too hard.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:55.210
We'll stop for today and get a fire started.

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:56.970
Tonight, we camp here.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:01.300
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:00.730
Really?

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:03.680
Homare-san?

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:04.580
Hm?

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:07.350
Why did you bring me with you?

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:11.170
You have a deliberate
nature and adapt quickly.

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:15.870
I think you're the most suited
for the survival mindset, Mutsu.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:17.360
M-Me?

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:20.280
<i>I really don't think that's true...</i>

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:24.250
In that case, I'm a little worried
about the two we left behind.

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:26.880
The two that aren't suited
for a survival situation.

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:30.490
Oh, my! What a beautiful mushroom!

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:31.870
Fly Agaric (Poisonous)

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:33.730
It looks delicious!

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:36.000
Oh, no! I set it on fire!

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:39.590
It's so dark!

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:41.610
I can't go pee...

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:44.200
Dependability level: zero.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.410
I-It's gotten dark...

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:49.290
Homare-san, you seem pretty worried.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:52.380
I-I'm not particularly worried.

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:54.030
I just can't help thinking about it...

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:54.030
How is it?

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:55.060
It's cold!

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.760
Oh! What a coincidence,
running into you here.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:14.140
We just happened to be taking
a walk over there.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:17.000
That was a completely contrived entrance!

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.630
Guess there's no helping it.

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:22.900
All four of us will camp out here tonight.

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:25.490
Thank you, Homare!

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:28.810
What? You came empty-handed?

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:31.450
I only brought enough
dried rock shells for two.

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:33.560
Well, I mean...

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:38.280
What're you doing?

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:39.810
I'm making a roof.

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:42.270
By making use of branches and things,

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:45.290
you can make a shelter, like they do
for emergency evacuations.

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:47.150
It's called "first bivouac."

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:49.410
Make sure you remember, Homare.

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:50.850
I will, Papa!

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:57.060
What's with all this?

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:59.650
We found it nearby earlier.

00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:01.650
It looks like a net used by fishermen.

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:02.630
I see...

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:04.300
Pull that side tighter.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:04.980
Okay.

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:06.470
We're sleeping in this net?

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:10.060
I-It's cramped...

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:13.390
But there are all kinds
of bugs in the leaf litter, so...

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:22.130
Say, what do you think
about naming this island?

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:25.770
Wouldn't it already have a name?

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:28.530
It's just that we have no way of knowing it...

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:30.350
Just a temporary name. For us.

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:32.030
What about "Kujou Island"?

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:33.620
That's your last name.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:37.790
It sounds like a place in a mystery
where an incident occurs.

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:42.990
If we take the beginnings 
of all of our names...

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:44.570
Ahomushi (Idiot's) Island!

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:45.800
Rejected!

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.280
Really...

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.800
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:53.180
Shion-san! Asuka-san! It's time to wake up.

00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:55.770
Wow! Awesome! That's crab!

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:57.770
Apparently, you can eat it
just like that, whole.

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:00.980
It's quite fragrant and delicious.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:04.490
Once we've finished eating,
we should explore the area.

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:05.280
Explore?

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:07.360
There was a place for boats!

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:10.320
It's possible that there are people nearby!

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:11.260
Huh?

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:12.740
Here, on the island?

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:16.220
So, it could be... we're saved?

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:18.180
Yes! Let's go look!

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:20.410
And not just here, we'll scour
every inch of the island!

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:25.380
Let's use a fan-shaped search pattern.

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:26.980
We'll each take different directions,

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:29.920
go 1,000 steps in a straight line,
then turn and come back.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:31.340
I see.

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:33.010
Okay! Let's go.

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:33.640
Okay!

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:36.570
Will you be all right? Can you count to 1,000?

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:38.470
How dumb do you think I am?

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:41.480
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:40.930
Is that so?

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.150
245... 246...

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:46.480
247... 248...

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:50.110
Let's see... given one stride is about 60 cm,

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:52.490
1,000 steps would be about 600 meters...

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:56.530
255... 256... 257...

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:58.930
Huh? That's...

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:08.800
293... 294...

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:12.360
295... 296... 297...

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:13.350
29—

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:16.050
Ta-dah!

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.260
I found yuzu!

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:21.370
My grandma has some in her
field, so I knew it right away!

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:22.650
Oh, it's so familiar!

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:24.690
Yuzu is primarily a Japanese crop.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:27.890
That raises the likelihood that
this is a Japanese island.

00:08:27.890 --> 00:08:29.440
I think so, too!

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:32.310
Shion-san isn't back yet...

00:08:32.310 --> 00:08:35.200
Yeah. I hope she isn't lost...

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:37.060
E-Everyone!

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:38.820
A-A house!

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:40.080
I found a house!

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:44.500
This way, right?

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:45.830
There might be people.

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:46.920
That's great!

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:48.710
First thing is to borrow the phone!

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:51.300
Here it is!

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:06.970
It's true it's a house...

00:09:06.970 --> 00:09:09.300
But it's all falling apart!

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:11.240
I'm sure they've just stepped out for a bit.

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:12.650
Excuse me!

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:15.030
I-I don't think there's anyone here.

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:17.310
No. This is an important find.

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:21.660
Over half of it has collapsed...

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:23.750
Huh? You're going in?

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:25.070
It's dangerous!

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:25.750
Don't worry.

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:28.290
There's basically no roof.

00:09:28.550 --> 00:09:30.080
The floor's rotted away...

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:32.460
The supports and walls are leaning...

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:35.130
It's not livable at all.

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:36.810
If there was at least...

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:41.000
I hope Homare-san is all right.

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:42.330
Oh, right!

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:43.850
Let's try eating the yuzu!

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:46.570
It's hard. I can't peel it.

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:48.150
You can eat the peel, too.

00:09:50.030 --> 00:09:51.910
It's bitter! And sour!

00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:53.690
But it's edible.

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:55.460
Let me have a bite, too!

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:56.950
Everyone! It's amazing!

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:57.700
Huh?

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.200
Don't be too shocked.

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:02.260
Look!

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:04.040
Huh?

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:05.540
Scissors?

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:08.210
And they're super beat up...

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:12.090
They seem broken, and there's so much
rust, wouldn't they be hard to use?

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:14.240
No, not at all!

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:16.880
I've been wanting something metal.

00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:19.500
And just look at this shape...

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:21.970
It's ideal.

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:25.440
First, we break this hinge.

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:26.520
See?

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:29.020
See?

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:30.470
You don't see it?

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:31.520
<b>Wooden Hilt</b>

00:10:30.470 --> 00:10:31.940
It can turn into a knife!

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:37.310
And it's even got holes
for the fastening pins!

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:35.440
<b>Pin holes</b>

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:38.400
<b>Smooth Around the Pins</b>

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:38.400
<i>She really loves knives, doesn't she?</i>

00:10:37.310 --> 00:10:39.240
{this bleeds into the title screen} It's ideal! Perfect!

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:41.410
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:41.080
I see...

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:41.410
At any rate, finding this
was a stroke of good luck.

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:45.570
If you pick too many, they'll just rot, so...

00:10:45.570 --> 00:10:48.280
pick enough for a few days and
we'll come back to pick more later.

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:49.330
Got it!

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:54.620
Let's try climbing to the high
ground in the middle of the island.

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:57.330
There might be land nearby,

00:10:57.330 --> 00:10:59.050
and I'd like to see the shape
of the whole island.

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:05.730
We made it!

00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:10.580
I don't see anything.

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:13.580
So we really are in the middle of the ocean...

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:14.560
It seems so.

00:11:18.140 --> 00:11:19.340
That's...

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:21.600
Smoke?

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:28.870
Next time, Case 8:
 "Oasis Found?!"

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:29.970
<b>Oasis Found?!</b>
